Subject: RE: New carton sizes S2 / M3 / L4 from 2 Nov - master data and EWM

No need to scrap anything, Sofie. Decision: the old cartons are used up first=
. 2 Nov is the date from which S2, M3 and L4 are the standard in the master d=
ata, but Antwerp keeps packing into S1, M2 and L3 until the stock is empty. N=
othing goes back to the supplier.

The first delivery of new cartons for Antwerp is planned for Thu 29 Oct, so p=
lease keep bay 14 free from that day. Once an old size is finished, switch th=
at size to the new one.

For reference, the new sizes (internal dimensions):

New size | Replaces | Internal size (mm)
S2 | S1 | 300 x 200 x 150
M3 | M2 | 400 x 300 x 200
L4 | L3 | 600 x 400 x 300

